                <pb facs="1085" n="965" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg965"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">863.00 Revolution 1931/9: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Funchal</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Huddleston</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-04-11T14:00:00-05:00">April 11, 1931—2
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your telegram April 10, 4 p.m. The Department has been caused no embarrassment of
                    which it is aware and perceives no reason why an apology should be
                    necessary.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
